-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party references and their licenses
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

xv/messages.py
  The System Exclusive frame layout, the RQ1/DT1 command IDs, the model ID
  (00H 10H), the checksum rule, the four-byte parameter address map and the
  Identity Reply payload are transcribed as data from Roland's own
  documentation:

    "XV-2020 Owner's Manual", Roland Corporation, 2003.
    MIDI Implementation chapter, pp. 140-146.

xv/banks.py
  The Bank Select MSB / LSB / Program Change map for the internal banks is
  transcribed from the same manual (pp. 40-41 and p. 136).

  The SRX expansion-board allocation -- every board's MSB, LSB range and
  program-change range -- is transcribed from:

    Roland Supplemental Note SN 132, v3.00, Summer 2007,
    "Selecting Internal and SRX-Series Sounds Via MIDI",
    (C) 2005, 2006, 2007 Roland Corporation U.S.

  Cross-checked against the individual SRX-02/05/06/07/08 Owner's Manuals.

xv/bridge.py
  The throttled-output queue, the MultiIn merged-input facade and the
  rtmidi-backend-client leak fix are ported from the author's sibling
  projects, all GPL-2.0-or-later:

    s3ked      Copyright (C) 2026  s3ked contributors
    eosed      Copyright (C) 2026  eosed contributors
    k2kremote  Copyright (C) 2026  k2kremote contributors
    mpc2emu    Copyright (C) 2025-2026  mpc2emu contributors

xv/config.py, rxved/favorites.py, the legend widget and the parser
  These were copies of code that now lives in vinsynlib, the shared base of
  this family of terminal instrument browsers -- see README.md "Development
  checks" for how it is installed. vinsynlib was itself assembled from the
  copies these six projects carried, and is GPL-2.0-or-later:

    vinsynlib   Copyright (C) 2026  vinsynLib contributors
                (assembled from emorphed, ensqsqed, eosed, kwsed,
                 nanosyned, p2ked, s3ked and x5ded contributors)

tools/extract_catalog.py
  Reads, but does not redistribute, Roland's own files: the XV-2020 Editor
  for Windows (Roland Corporation, 2006), the XV-2020 Owner's Manual and the
  XV-2020 Patch Listing. Its output is patch, rhythm-set and performance
  names, which are Roland's; that output is NOT part of this distribution
  and is excluded by .gitignore. Each user generates it from their own
  copies of those files. See README.md.

